      "body": "## Problem\n\nIn `Sampler._sync_token_ids_across_tp`, the final-token-id `all_reduce` is gated only on `SYNC_TOKEN_IDS_ACROSS_TP` (env, default off) or non-empty `sampling_info.grammars`. It does not check the size of the sync group.\n\nUnder `tp=1` PP-only prefill, the TP group is a **single rank**, so the `MIN` all-reduce is a semantic no-op. However, issuing it still **lazily initializes the NCCL communicator**, which allocates device buffers. Under memory pressure that allocation can fail (observed: `Failed to CUDA calloc 536870912 bytes`), raising an unhandled NCCL error that crashes the scheduler (SIGQUIT) — even though the reduce itself was pointless.\n\nThis is the same class of issue as our earlier indexer OOM: a hidden over-allocation that only surfaces when headroom is tiny.\n\n## Fix\n\nSkip the all-reduce when the actual sync group has a single rank:\n\n```python\nif (\n    SYNC_TOKEN_IDS_ACROSS_TP or sampling_info.grammars\n) and dist.get_world_size(self.tp_sync_group) > 1:\n    torch.distributed.all_reduce(...)\n```\n\nThe guard reads the real process-group size (not static tp config), so:\n- single-rank group → no-op skipped (no communicator init, no allocation);\n- multi-rank group → identical behavior to today.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `self.tp_sync_group` is created at init from `get_tp_group()` (or `attn_tp_group` under DP-attention), so its size is fixed for the process lifetime.\n- No correctness impact: a one-rank MIN reduce is the identity.\n\n## Test\n\n- `python -m py_compile` on the file passes.\n- Local path (pp=8, tp=1) no longer hits the NCCL lazy-init allocation when grammars are present.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37892419196](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37892419196)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37892418852](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37892418852)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37892418959](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37892418959)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
